      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-04-11_WidnesExaminer_art0018" n="art0018">
        <head>REALISATION OF AN ESTArE.</head>
        <p>REALISATION OF AN ESTArE.</p>
        <p>Warrington Partnership Dispute</p>
        <p>At the Lancashire Chancery Court. sitting at Liver- pool on Monday, His Honour Vice-Chancellor Leigh- Clare made an order on the application of the plaintiff in the matter of Pemberton V. Mainwarin,g. The pirties were in partnership at Warrington as land jobbers and brick and tile makers. but the partnership was dissolved at the end of 1906. The plaintiff complained that the defendant was making no attempt to realise either the ground rents, building land, or brickworks which formed the estate of the partnership, and applied for the appointment of a receiver and an order of sale. Mr.Courthope Wilsonappeared for the plaintiff and Mr. Lawrence for the defendant, who urged that the dis- puted accounts between the parties should first be settled, an amount of £22,000 being involved. The Vice Chancellor made an order for the immedi- ate sale of the ground rents aid a direction for the selling, letting, or otherwise disposing of the rest of the property in such a manner as the Registrar of the Court may determine, with liberty to either party to bring in proposals, and with liberty to the defendant to bid at any sale.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-04-11_WidnesExaminer_art0019" n="art0019">
        <head>NASAL CATARRH St ASTHMA.</head>
        <p>NASAL CATARRH St ASTHMA.</p>
        <p>THEIR COMPLETO IfOMEI CURE. POST FREE TO SUFFERERS WFIO APPLY AT ONCE.</p>
        <p>Just published, the second edition of a 1 page book fully describing Nasal Catarrh, Asthma and Chronic Bronchitis, and how these dangerous diseases may be completely cured at home. The most practical work ever issued, end should be in the hands of sufferers who desire to speedily cure themselves. This offer stands open for 30 days from this date. A post card giving your name and address will bring you the book free by return post. Address Dept. B. 341, Dr. Cassell's Co., I Ltd., Ayton Buildings, King at., %Vest, Manchester.</p>
