      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-04-11_WidnesExaminer_art0036" n="art0036">
        <head>WIN WICK FREE CHURCH.</head>
        <p>WIN WICK FREE CHURCH.</p>
        <p>Annual Meeting.</p>
        <p>In connection with the above church the annual tea and congregational meeting was held on Monday after- noon and evening. There were both at the tea and meeting a fairly large number present. I riends from Warrington putting in an appearance. The lady friends attached to the church presided at the tea tables which had been neatly decorated and assisted in giving appetite to the delicacies provided. After tea a general meeting was held, Mr. C. E. Parker (President of ,the Warrington Free Church Council) occupying the chair. After a few well chosen and ,ncouraging remarks from the Chairman inspiring 'dresses were delivered by the Revs. J. S. Hughes and % Matthews and also by Messrs. E. England and E. 'rice Jones, and Mrs. Parker on Free Church work its meaning, which were much enjoyed by the audience. The reports of . the Church are very encouraging as the numbers of its adherents are steadily increasing,</p>
