      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-04-11_WidnesExaminer_art0042" n="art0042">
        <head>HOME TO SUPERSEDE RESTAURANTS.</head>
        <p>HOME TO SUPERSEDE RESTAURANTS.</p>
        <p>Those who can read the social barometer assure us, says a writer in the Lady, that a great change in social customs is approaching. The 'restaurant proprietor may consider that the glass is going down, the admirer of the domes- tic virtues that it is goiug up; but, anyhow, the social weather experts say we are in for a spell of dining at home. Yes, the restaurant fever is abating. Home is not to be the place where we keep the servants, but the place where we lunch and dine and shew hospitality to our friends. The intimate and exclusive hospitality of the private house is to have a chance.</p>
        <p>r. a.. Mrs. Sure, of Bur.. both cured by Dr. Williams' Pink Pals. "Some time ago," said Mr. Snee to a reporter, "I was suddenly taken ill as the result of a Cold, and had to give up work. Life lost all interest for me and I became quite melancholy.</p>
        <p>RHEUMATISM RAGING. "Later on Rheumatic pains attacked my back and arms. At every movement an agony seized me, increasing in intensity until I could not hold myself upright. One day, as I was stooping, a sharp pain ran along my spine and I fainted. " Common cures for Rheumatism did not relieve me, and my nervous system gave way under the strains of my sufferings; every noise irritated</p>
        <p>"My wife urged me to try Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People, and little dreaming that I should be cured I took a course. After a few boxes the inflammation left my joints, and the pains in my back and limbs disappeared. I became strong and well again and soon returned to work, fit and happy." EDS WIFE PROSTRATED BY ANEMIA. Mrs. Snee then said :—" I advised my husband to take Dr. Williams' Pink Pills, because when I was perilously ill through antemia they cured me. I was terribly weak and -bloodless and my heart palpitated so that I could not mount the stairs without collapsing. I lost appetite and was tortured with acute Indigestion. My face became deathly white, I lost flesh rapidly, and was tormented with nervousness and neuralgia. I had given up hope of ever being happy and well again, when a friend persuaded me to try Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People. I gained great relief from the first box, and after I bad taken five or six boxes I was enjoying the very best health. Dr. Williams' Pink Pills gave me great strength ; took away all nervousness, backaches and neuralgia i and left me with a clear and healthy complexion."</p>
