      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-04-11_WidnesExaminer_art0086" n="art0086">
        <head>ANOTHER FROM NEWTON-LEWILLOWS.</head>
        <p>ANOTHER FROM NEWTON-LE- WILLOWS.</p>
        <p>We have already printed many statements dealing with the same subject as doss the following ; here is still another, the experience of a resident in Newton-le- Willows. It is noteworthy that every one of these statements has in it a ring of truth and openness that cannot fail to impress us with its absolute truthfulness. They have brought happiness and health to many homes here in. Mr. Andrew Williams, 158, Wargrave-road, Newton4e- Willows is very well known about here, and we feel sure many will appreciate his kindness in making the following statement and consenting to its publication, for it will give those who suffer as he did an opportunity of benefiting by his experience. " I have been using Doan's pills and they have done remarkably well. I had previously used another remedy, but I am more satisfied with the result of Doan's—the other medicine was not to be compared with them ; I was warp rised how good the pills proved to be. "For three yesrs I had suffered with my back, having shooting pains across the kidneys ; when stooped to lift anything, it always started my back aching. The urinary secretions were thick and painful. "1 have felt splendid, however, since using Doan's pills ; they have quitei rectified my kidney trouble. I've advised many to try the pills. (Signed) Andrew Williams." Doan's Backache Kidney Pills are two shillings -and ninepence per box (six boxes for thirteen shillings and ninepence). Of all chemists and stores, or post free, direct from Foster-McClellan Co., 8, Wells-street, Oxford-street, London, W. You are sure to get the right medicine if you ask distinctly for DOAN'S.</p>
      </div>
