      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-04-11_WidnesExaminer_art0088" n="art0088">
        <head>1907.</head>
        <p>1907.</p>
        <p>A GREAT CORRECTIVE.</p>
        <p>NOT A CURE-ALL.</p>
        <p>We do not claim that Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills are a Cure-all, but as a corrective for all complaints arising from disorders, of the blood, the stomach, liver and kidneys, they are unexcelled. As, how- ever nine out of every ten ailments are due to these 'auses, Dr. Morse's In- lian Root Pills fill a want in every household. In- deed, they are a house- 'iold necessity, as effee- _lye with the strong as with the most delicate, and compounded to meet the requirements of every age—from infancy to advanced life. They are a safe, sure, and reliable remedy, and will prevent many of the complaints so common if taken once or twice a week to keep the system a healthy condition.</p>
        <p>For all complaints aris- ing from imperfect digestion and impure blood these pills are an invaluable remedy. For sale by all Chemists and Stores, price 1/ per bottle, or 6 bottles for 6/6, or will be sent by the Proprietors, The W. H. Comstock Co., Ltd., Farringdon Avenue, London, E.C. t flee sample will be forwarded on receipt of Id. stamp.</p>
        <p>Knocked Down by Motor Cycle. On Sunday afternoon a deaf and dumb cld weinan named Mary Milieu, 4, Jolley's-yard, was crossing. Knutsford-road when a motor cycle ridden by Coun- cillor Clowes Baxendale, 3, Mealhouse•lane, Atherton, approached. The driver sounded the alarm and applied the brakes, but was unable to pull up before knocking the wiman down. Fortunately the machine did not go over her, tholurh she indicated that her thigh had been injured,, while she was much shaken. Mr. Baxendale's companion, William Heaton, 31, Market-street, Atherton, went off on his own motor cycle for Dr. Collins, who attended Mrs. Mallett and had her removed in the horse ambulance to the Infirmary. Though the woman was not suffering from any serious injury Dr. Brown deemed it advisa- able to detain her.</p>
